 34S     34S(G,G'),(POL G,G')          1984BE26,1978BE46         ENSDF    202609
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34S 2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34S  c  Nuclear resonance fluorescence (NRF) measurements:                     
 34S  c  1984Be26: {+34}S(pol |g,|g') with 18-MeV unpolarized and linearly      
 34S 2c  polarized bremsstrahlung beams from the 65-MeV electron linac at the   
 34S 3c  University of Giessen. Targets were mixtures of H{-3}BO{-3}, C, MgO,   
 34S 4c  Si, and S. |g rays were detected using four Ge(Li) detectors at        
 34S 5c  azimuthal angles of 0|', 90|', 180|', and 270|' relative to the        
 34S 6c  polarization plane of the linearly polarized beam. Measured E|g, I|g,  
 34S 7c  and |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, decay widths to the ground state        
 34S 8c  (|G{-0}), and electric/magnetic characters from azimuthal asymmetry of 
 34S 9c  scattered |g rays.                                                     
 34S  c  1978Be46: {+34}S(|g,|g') with an 18-MeV electron bremsstrahlung beam   
 34S 2c  from the 65-MeV electron linac at the University of Giessen on a 1-g   
 34S 3c  self-supporting 77.9%-enriched {+34}S target. |g rays were detected    
 34S 4c  using a Ge(Li) detector at 125|' relative to the bremsstrahlung beam.  
 34S 5c  Measured E|g, I|g, and integrated (|g,|g') scattering cross sections.  
 34S 6c  Deduced levels, J, and decay widths to the ground state (|G{-0}). Also 
 34S 7c  see 1977BeYD.                                                          
 34S  cG E$From level energy differences.                                       
 34S  cG M$From measured |g(|q) and azimuthal asymmetry of scattered |g rays.   
 34S  cL E,J,T$From 1978Be46, unless otherwise noted. Due to the low momentum   
 34S 2cL transfer of photons, primary dipole and to a lesser extent quadrupole, 
 34S 3cL transitions are induced. For 0+ g.s. target, most likely J=1 states are
 34S 4cL populated. The decay widths to the ground state (|G{-0}) are deduced by
 34S 5cL authors assuming J=1 and 100% decay to g.s.                            
 34S  cL E(A),J(A),T(A)$From 1984Be26 based on |g multipolarities deduced from  
 34S 2cL |g(|q) and azimuthal asymmetry of scattered |g rays.                   
